<title>UK: World 1996/97 cotton output revised touch higher.</title>
<headline>World 1996/97 cotton output revised touch higher.</headline>
<dateline>LIVERPOOL, England 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cotton Outlook revised its 1996/97 world cotton output estimate up to 18.99 million tonnes in November from 18.86 million estimated in October.</p>
<p>In 1995/96 the total was estimated at 19.90 million tonnes.</p>
<p>U.S. output was forecast at 4.07 against the October estimate of 3.96 million tonne and 3.89 million in 1995/96. China's production was seen unchanged at 3.80 million but still down on 4.76 million in 1995/96.</p>
<p>Estimates were as follows, in thousand tonnes -</p>
<p>				 1995/96		   1996/97</p>
<p>			     Nov	 Oct	 Nov	   Oct</p>
